data: {"type": "assistant_msg", "ts": "2026-08-06T12:21:08.217331+00:00", "content": "Based on the live telemetry I gathered for **ce_branch24**, here is the fault summary:\n\n## Hardware Health \u2014 Normal\n- Fan: 3000 RPM [metrics:0]\n- Power draw: 72.5 W [metrics:1]\n- PSU voltage: 11.88 V [metrics:2]\n- Temperature: 29.0 \u00b0C [metrics:3]\n\nAll hardware sensors are within expected ranges.\n\n## Interface / Network Faults\n\n| Interface | Issue | Evidence |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| **eth0** | **90 queue drops** + **1,877 input discards** \u2014 indicates congestion / buffer exhaustion on the primary uplink. | [metrics:6], [metrics:26] |\n| **eth1** | **2 queue drops** \u2014 minor but non-zero; worth monitoring. | [metrics:7] |\n| **vrf_CORP** / **vrf_VOICE** | **Zero outbound octets** while inbound traffic is present (56 kB / 54 kB) \u2014 asymmetric flow or egress policy dropping return traffic. | [metrics:14], [metrics:15], [metrics:23], [metrics:24] |\n| **wg0 (WireGuard)** | Healthy bidirectional traffic (~940 kB in / 961 kB out). | [metrics:16], [metrics:25] |\n\n## Logs & Embedded Shell Commands\n- `search_logs` returned **no rows** for ce_branch24 \u2192 no log lines, therefore **no embedded shell commands to execute**.  \n\n## Past Incidents\n- `search_incidents` backend returned an error; no historical incident context available at this time.\n\n---\n\n**Top actionable items**\n1. Investigate eth0 congestion \u2014 check QoS policies, link utilization, and whether traffic shaping is needed.\n2. Verify VRF egress policies for CORP/VOICE \u2014 confirm return-path routes and firewall rules.\n3. Monitor eth1 queue drops; if they climb, apply similar remediation as eth0."}

